# Anthropic credentials for both AI tools (deck evaluator + website reviewer).
# The SDK resolves credentials itself, in order: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ->
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN -> the active `ant auth login` CLI profile -> Workload
# Identity Federation env vars -> the default profile on disk. So for local
# dev you can leave this file's ANTHROPIC_API_KEY blank entirely and just run
# `ant auth login` once instead — no env var needed. In Vercel's dashboard,
# an API key is the practical choice (see README) since Vercel functions
# can't do an interactive CLI login.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Required outside Vercel (local dev, this sandbox, or any other host):
# point this at a real Chromium binary. Install one locally with
# `npx playwright install chromium`, then set this to the path it reports.
# On Vercel, leave this unset — lib/screenshot.ts detects the VERCEL env var
# (set automatically by the platform) and uses @sparticuz/chromium instead.
PLAYWRIGHT_EXECUTABLE_PATH=
